 "data": {
  "explanation": "theta (delta=+1,e=+1: <d>_cl -> <d>_ad^-1, U_q -> +Pi_q) matches at every pair, eps=-1 never does. At N=7 the even cubic characters have chi(q) = zeta_3^{+-1} != +-1 and both mixed dictionaries fail (witnessed failure of Pi_q^-1 with delta=+1), as prop:s05-sign(c) predicts. The genuine Rosati dictionary theta^Ros (T_l -> <l>_ad T_l, <d> -> <d>_ad, U_q -> Pi_q^-1) also matches at every pair: it is the eigensystem-level shadow of prop:s05-AL (theta vs theta^Ros indistinguishable at one level; separated only by naturality in p-power levels, prop:s05-sign(d)), so this is no contradiction. The naive (delta,e)=(-1,-1) with T_l -> T_l fails by the T_l-relation (lem:s05-consistency(a)). At N=5 only the trivial and the quadratic even character occur (the order-4 characters are odd), so chi(q)=+-1, delta is invisible and (c) imposes nothing; (+1,-1) still fails there, because Pi_q^-1 = -Pi_q on the chi(q)=-1 part (a sign, not the exponent relation). The plan's criterion ord(q mod N) not in {1,2} is not sufficient: informative needs q^2 != +-1 mod N (even chi only).",
